I don't remember now how I found these. My best guess: either a
post in this newsgroup, or a web search.

The only other Qt option I know, at least for Mac OS X, is

    Qt_compact

When you turn this option on:

    Qt_compact=1

the display loses all the status information above the map. This
almost doubles the amount of map space you can display at once,
a possible solution to your no-vertical-scroll problem. I don't
use this options, principally because it loses the status display,
and I don't know of any way to obtain that status information.


